# Cleanup and Relocation of Cosma Configuration

The user wants to remove all traces of the Cosma installation from the root of their Obsidian vault (`Ecosistema_Fintech_Global`) because it caused configuration issues with the graph. I will move all Cosma-related files to a separate directory called `cosma_workspace` within the project (or a sibling, but I'll stick to a subdirectory first unless specified otherwise, or perhaps a sibling folder to be safer).

## Proposed Changes

### [Cosma Cleanup]

I will move the following files/folders from the vault root:

- [cosma.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma.yml) [MOVE]
- [config.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/config.yml) [MOVE]
- [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/package.json) [MOVE]
- [package-lock.json](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/package-lock.json) [MOVE]
- `export/` [MOVE]
- `node_modules/` [DELETE] (to be reinstalled if needed in the new location)

#### [NEW] [cosma_workspace/](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma_workspace)
A new directory to house Cosma-related configurations.

#### [MODIFY] [cosma_workspace/cosma.yml](file:///c:/Users/Antonio/OneDrive/Escritorio/Ecosistema_Fintech_Global/cosma_workspace/cosma.yml)
Update the `entry` setting to point to the parent directory (the vault root) so Cosma can still analyze the markdown files without being located at the root.

